nodecode-muse-harness is a rewrite of SnoobieJunes's SnoobieJunes/hermes-muse-harness:

  https://github.com/SnoobieJunes/hermes-muse-harness
  commit 5cc2d060dee651345c75a75e4a52abb2272462be

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Auston (SnoobieJunes) (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the whole MSP client. What the Hermes plugin did in Python --
start `muse serve`, speak newline-delimited JSON-RPC on its stdin and stdout,
run initialize, session/start and turn/start, answer MSP's approval requests
with the mode's decision, collect the agent message's deltas and read
turn/completed -- this cell does in Lisp through the kernel's process seam,
and the Hermes secrets store becomes one environment variable the section
names. Left out: the plugin's JSON envelope (session id, approvals, billing
as fields) is answered as the turn's text, with a failure line when the
turn did not complete and a note when the retry billed pay-as-you-go; the
plugin's provider switch (meta, local, echo) is fixed to meta, which is the
only one its tool exposed; and the reader thread's per-frame byte cap moved
into the frame reader itself. Nothing of the original's code, and no Python,
is bundled.
